==English==

===Etymology===
Abbreviation of {{m|en||[[on]] [[speculation]]}}.

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# In hope of success, using one's best guess
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1889|author=Banjo Paterson|title=[[s:Clancy of the Overflow|Clancy of the Overflow]]
|passage=I had written him a letter which I had, for want of better<br>Knowledge, sent to where I met him down the Lachlan, years ago,<br>He was shearing when I knew him, so I sent the letter to him,<br>Just '''on spec''', addressed as follows, “Clancy, of The Overflow”.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial|business|of creating a work}} With the hope of selling it, as opposed to on commission {{gloss|for hire}}.
#: ''I'm writing an article '''on spec'''. I hope some magazine will buy it.''
#* '''1955''', [[w:Rex Stout|Rex Stout]], "The Next Witness", in [[w:Three Witnesses (book)|''Three Witnesses'']], October 1994 [[w:Bantam Books|Bantam]] edition, {{ISBN|0553249592}}, page 36:
#*: "Why doubt his guilt?"
#*: Wolfe's shoulders went up a fraction of an inch, and down again. "Divination. Contrariety."
#*: "I see." Unger pursed his midget mouth, which didn't need pursing. "You're shooting at it '''on spec'''."

